products are used in various electronic products in a range of applications for the industrial Internet of Things (IoT), including connected home and security, industrial automation and control, smart metering and agriculture, smart street lighting, renewable energy, electric vehicle supply equipment, industrial wearables and equipment, commercial building automation, consumer electronics, asset tracking, and medical instrumentation; and commercial IoT applications, including smart buildings and lighting, access controls, asset tracking, electronic shelf labels, theft protection, power tools, and enterprise access points. The company's smart home applications comprise smart home cameras, locks, gateways, residential lighting, window shades/blinds, heating, ventilation, air conditioning, switches, smoke/CO detectors, sensors, and home security panels; and connected health applications, including diabetes management, consumer health and fitness, elderly care, patient monitoring, and activity tracking, as well as provides wireless microcontrollers products. It sells its products through its direct sales force, as well as a network of independent sales representatives and distributors. The company was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Matthew Johnson | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $407K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $34K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $42K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Silicon Laboratories, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.4B market cap on $785M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -9% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $66M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -12.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -72.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 902% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":9.022882255927067},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","ca